From 78d4723aa9c526867af3bb82b37dc580a9f960e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:44:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Remove a self join only when one of its subjects depends on
 the join references

A join of a logical source with itself on the same references was always
replaced by the parent subject of the same row. That is right only when all
the rows with the same join values give the same parent subject, or give the
same child subject, predicate and graph; otherwise each row is joined with
every row with the same join values (RMLTC0033a, kg-construct/rml-core).
GTFS-Madrid-Bench, STOP_TIMES joined with itself on trip_id: 2,364 triples
instead of 43,008 at scale 1.

The join is kept unless the parent subject, or the child subject with its
predicate and graph (constants allowed), is a template or a reference whose
references are all join references. Test: test/self-join.
